# This file contains the keystore information used to sign your app.
# For production builds, you MUST create a copy named 'key.properties' (note: this file is gitignored)
# and fill in the actual values.
#
# IMPORTANT: The certificate hash used to sign the release APK MUST match the one registered
# in Firebase Console. If they don't match, Google Sign-In will fail in production.
#
# Steps to set up:
# 1. Create your release keystore if you don't have one:
#    keytool -genkey -v -keystore ~/tiffin_release.jks -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000 -alias tiffin_key
#
# 2. Get the SHA-1 fingerprint of your release key:
#    keytool -list -v -keystore ~/tiffin_release.jks
#    (Look for "SHA1:" line)
#
# 3. Copy this file to 'key.properties' and fill in the values below
#
# 4. Register the SHA-1 fingerprint in Firebase Console:
#    - Go to Firebase Project Settings > Android App
#    - Add your SHA-1 fingerprint
#    - Download the updated google-services.json
#
# 5. Place your keystore file in the android folder and reference it below

storeFile=../tiffin_release.jks
storePassword=YOUR_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD
keyAlias=tiffin_key
keyPassword=YOUR_KEY_PASSWORD
